       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and, in overdose, prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that ceiling.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the usual maximum.\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose. Some patients start at 2.5 mg.\n- **Another dose or frequency**, if I misread the order.\n\nIf you really do want 30 mg, for example because of a specific clinical rationale, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
